%% Instagram Scanning Process - Error Detection and Handling
%% Classifies errors and determines retry strategy

flowchart TD
    Error([Error Detected]) --> ClassifyError{Error<br/>Type?}

    ClassifyError -->|Network| NetworkError[Network Error<br/>- Timeout<br/>- Connection refused<br/>- DNS failure]
    ClassifyError -->|Access| AccessError[Access Error<br/>- Login required<br/>- Private account<br/>- Content deleted]
    ClassifyError -->|Instagram| InstagramError[Instagram Error<br/>- Malformed URL<br/>- Expired signature<br/>- Rate limiting]
    ClassifyError -->|System| SystemError[System Error<br/>- Browser crash<br/>- CDP failure<br/>- Memory error]

    NetworkError --> LogError[Log Error Details<br/>- Error type<br/>- Error message<br/>- Timestamp]
    AccessError --> LogError
    InstagramError --> TrackInstagram[Track Instagram Issue<br/>- has_instagram_issues=TRUE<br/>- instagram_issue_notes<br/>- Separate from code bugs]
    SystemError --> LogError

    TrackInstagram --> UpdateStatus
    LogError --> UpdateStatus[Update Entry Status<br/>- cdn_acquisition_status=error<br/>- download_status=error<br/>- Store error details]

    UpdateStatus --> ShouldRetry{Retryable<br/>Error?}
    ShouldRetry -->|Yes| ScheduleRetry[Suggest Rescan<br/>- User notification<br/>- Retry counter]
    ShouldRetry -->|No| MarkFailed[Mark as Failed<br/>- Permanent failure<br/>- Needs manual review]

    ScheduleRetry --> ErrorHandled([Error Handled])
    MarkFailed --> ErrorHandled

    style Error fill:#FF6B6B
    style ErrorHandled fill:#FFD700
    style TrackInstagram fill:#87CEEB
